        "githubCommitAuthorEmail": "friemerx@gmail.com",
        "githubCommitMessage": "fix(blog): build-time hero manifest instead of runtime fs check\n\nThe hero fallback called fs.existsSync with a dynamic path under public/.\nNext's output file tracing cannot resolve dynamic paths, so it bundled the\nentire public/images subtree into every serverless function importing\nlib/blog.ts — api/md hit 289 MB, over Vercel's 250 MB limit, failing the\npreview deploy.\n\nscripts/build-route-index.mjs (already in the prebuild slot) now also\nwrites data/blog-hero-manifest.json — a sorted list of every file under\npublic/images/blog as URL paths. lib/blog.ts imports that JSON statically\nand tests Set membership; local paths outside /images/blog/ are trusted\n(pre-fallback behavior). Semantics verified identical to the fs check:\n80 present, 114 fall back. New images are picked up on the next build via\nprebuild regeneration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
